# Test: send and receive allow-lists (absent, partial, empty) and combined send allow + to govern delivery, refusal messages, counters, and commit validation.
# QUESTION: (S7) for an external endpoint `sender` declaring `bgp:update` and `bgp:refresh`,
# do absent, partial (`allow [ bgp:update ]`), and empty (`allow none`) send allow-lists
# produce 0, 1, and 2 refusals on `ze_bus_send_refused_total` with the exact allow-list
# refusal message and fix line, while an undeclared `allow [ bgp:raw ]` is refused at
# validate listing what `sender` declared; (S8) for `collector` with absent, partial
# (`allow [ bgp:state ]`), and empty (`allow none`) receive allow-lists, does `collector`
# record both, `bgp:state` only, and nothing while Loc-RIB keeps `edge1`'s route in all
# three; and (S9) with `send { allow [ bgp:update ]; to [ /bgp/group/transit ]; }`, does an
# unscoped update reach `t1` and `t2` only (not `edge1` or `lab`), is `bgp:refresh` refused
# by the allow-list (not `send > to`), and is adding `message bgp:refresh { to ... }`
# refused at validate naming both lines? A unit test cannot decide this because it spans
# live BGP sessions, wire UPDATE/refresh delivery, Prometheus counters, and live Loc-RIB.
#
# VALIDATES: spec-explicit-plugin-and-attach-config S7, S8, S9 / AC-5, AC-6.
# PREVENTS: allow-lists failing to enforce absent/partial/empty modes, miscounting
# refusals, starving sibling receivers on `receive > allow`, or combining `send > allow`
# with `send > to` incorrectly.

option=timeout:value=180s
option=env:var=ZE_CONFIG_DIR:value=.
option=env:var=XDG_DATA_HOME:value=.
option=env:var=ze.ssh.password:value=testpass

stdin=init-answers:terminator=EOF_INIT
admin
testpass
127.0.0.1
$PORT2
EOF_INIT

